<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Freising</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Freising is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isar">Isar</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corbinian">Saint Corbinian</a> worked there around 720, and in 739 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a> made it the seat of a bishopric, whose prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled a small territory until 1802; the see moved to Munich in 1821. The nearby Weihenstephan brewery traces its origins to a medieval abbey.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/freising.jpg" alt="Freising" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Doktor Oli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Domberg_FS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
